WEBVTT

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:14.120
Colors

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:18.660
Colors

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:50.750
We've got trouble, everyone!

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:52.500
Is it poop?!

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:53.450
Huh?

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:57.500
Why would it be poop, Sat-chan?

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.540
I was joking.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:01.660
Anyway, Yui...

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:03.450
I found these on the ground!

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:05.040
Weird glasses!

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.080
What the heck?

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.160
No, I mean!

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:09.200
There's trouble! It's a panda-

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.120
I mean, a cat!

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.290
There's a cat that looks like a panda!

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.500
Come on, would you take this seriously?

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.790
You, too, Kotoha!

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:26.000
But that's not trouble at all.

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:28.450
Listen, Yui!

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:32.450
We are the Colors - we keep the peace in our town!

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:36.200
Don't you have any bigger cases for us, Leader?

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:37.580
A cat!

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:39.950
There's a cat that looks like a panda!

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:42.290
Okay, okay, fine.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:44.910
Draw a picture so we can see what it looks like.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:45.790
Okay!

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:49.080
Done!

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:50.910
Look at this, Sat-chan.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.330
Let's see here.

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:56.750
I-it's a monster! 

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.330
A complete and utter monster!

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:00.410
Isn't it exciting?

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.580
It's beyond exciting!

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:05.660
We're gonna kill it?

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.160
N-no, we can't kill it!

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:11.410
But monsters like this need to be killed hard.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:14.120
So can we capture it, Leader?

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:16.750
Yes, that! Let's do that!

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:18.080
Okay!

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:20.040
Operation Catch the Monster Cat... 

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.370
is a go!

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:22.540
Yeah!

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:24.700
Haven't seen a monster like this.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:28.080
And hey, I know you need information, 

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.410
but it's cheating to go to the police for help

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.410
with your pretend hero games, you know.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.000
It's not "pretend," Saito.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:38.000
You don't know anything, Saito.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.750
Shut up, you snot-nosed brats!

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.750
I'm busy here!

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.750
I don't have time to play along with your little games, so...

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:45.580
leave...

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:46.370
me...

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:47.120
alone!

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.160
I'm sorry.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.160
She's the only decent kid of the bunch.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:55.950
That actually makes this harder.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:02.080
I haven't seen a monster like your drawing.

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:04.870
But I do have information about a cat

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:04.870
that looks like a panda.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:05.950
Really?!

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:09.250
Lately, a lot of people are coming in...

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:12.200
To report a panda-like cat stealing their stuff.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.620
In other words, it's a cat burglar.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.120
And so, if you can catch it...

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:21.200
it might lead to keeping the peace in our town.

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:24.330
A cat burglar!

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:26.910
This is a real case!

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:29.910
Note: Ameyoko Shopping Street - the market street of Ueno.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:29.910
Okay, first, let's search Shopping Street!

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.790
It's probably vicious. We'll have to be careful.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.250
Saito!

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:37.120
Huh?

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:38.790
Well done.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:41.540
Thanks.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.450
Ameyoko

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:45.870
Hello? Cat burglar!

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:48.540
Monster, where are you?

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:51.450
Specializing in

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:51.450
Full Body Massage 

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:51.450
2,900 Yen / Hour

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:51.450
Get out here, you monster cat!

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:02.000
Underground

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:02.000
Food Area

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.040
We can't find it anywhere.

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:25.830
What are you doing? You're supposed to follow me!

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:28.120
Huh? But what are YOU doing?

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:33.620
Well, you see, I'm going down

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:33.620
to the cat's eye level to make my sear-

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:37.830
Koto-chan, Koto-chan! You're stepping on me!

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:38.950
I know.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:40.080
I guess you would!

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.950
I've always wanted to try this.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.450
You're too twisted!

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:48.160
All those video games you're always playing

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:48.160
are warping your personality!

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:50.910
Don't talk like games are a bad influence.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.950
I have always been like this.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.080
That's even worse!

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:00.700
Sat-chan, Kotoha! Look!

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:02.160
Weird glasses...

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.660
They're creepy!

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:07.080
Hey, Colors!

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:10.700
What do you think of these glasses? Cool, right?

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.580
They're just like the ones I found at our hideout!

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:16.080
Hey, you're right - they are!

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:17.580
Pops!

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:22.330
By any chance, were a pair of those glasses

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:22.330
stolen by a panda-like cat?

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:26.250
Wow, Koto-chan. You're well informed.

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:30.290
That's right. That cat sure is a menace!

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:32.870
Really.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:34.160
I've got it.

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:35.660
What did you get?

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:36.750
Kotoha?

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:41.080
I've beat this game!

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:47.910
Wow, you're a really bad artist.

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:52.200
You actually caught him.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:56.410
You know what? Something he stole was in our hideout!

00:07:56.700 --> 00:08:00.870
So Kotoha thought maybe the cat

00:07:56.700 --> 00:08:00.870
was living in our hideout, too!

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:04.250
So we followed that theory and had a stakeout!

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:06.620
And you caught him...

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:12.500
Alright, then, girls. You keep him.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:13.870
What?!

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:18.540
If you hand him over to me,

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:18.540
he'll have to leave our town forever.

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:19.910
But...

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:23.120
Looks like he's pretty attached to you already.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:25.950
So train him. Make sure he doesn't cause any trouble.

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:29.160
Cats are citizens of our town, too, aren't they?

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:32.700
And what is your mission again?

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:35.950
To keep the peace of our town!

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:38.120
And its animals!

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:43.000
That's right! That's what I always thought!

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.290
Me, too!

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.450
I wanted to kill it, though.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:49.410
So what do we do? Take it back to the hideout and...

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:51.950
Instead of killing it,

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:51.950
we'll train it to be a professional killer.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:53.540
First we need to name it!

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:55.450
Too easy.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:57.080
One less thing for me to do.

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:04.790
So you'll be paying for its food.

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:06.790
Thank you, Saito-san!

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:07.750
Well done!

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:09.080
What?!

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:29.700
Oh, Colonel Monochrome! Welcome home!

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:33.910
Annoying little punks

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:33.910
Ah, too cute!

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.080
What is it, Colonel? 

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:38.290
Are you stealing again?

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:39.910
Sheesh.

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:43.160
The belly band from a manga?

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:46.120
Bring me something better.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:50.410
Like a weapon or something.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.040
Understand?

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:55.450
Here, Colonel!

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:57.370
I have some food!

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:03.330
Whoa, Colonel!

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.500
You must've been hungry!

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.000
Well take your time, and eat all you want!

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:11.660
What is it, Colonel?

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:14.580
There you go.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.410
A purr-fectly lazy kitty.

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:20.660
Colonel Monochrome really likes people, huh?

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:49.790
Isn't there anything?

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:52.040
Yui, whatcha looking for?

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.450
Well, the Colonel needs...

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:13.950
Um...

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:16.790
We are Colors!

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:19.450
Defenders of this town!

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:20.250
Sir!

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.250
This is to keep the peace.

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:25.200
Saito. You've gotten too corrupt.

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:27.250
Consider this unavoidable.

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:30.120
Hence the rocket launcher?

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:34.000
Saito! You need to explode! For the world's sake!

00:11:34.120 --> 00:11:35.290
Yeah, okay.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.700
Where did you get that, anyway?

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:41.080
It's probably just a replica.

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:43.950
Freeze! Move and we'll shoot!

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:00.000
Fire!

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:01.000
Seriously?

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:09.370
What's wrong, Kotoha?

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:10.870
It won't fire.

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:12.790
It must be a fake.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:13.910
A fake?!

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:16.580
Aw, man, a fake?

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:17.580
Ugh.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:18.660
Curse that Pops.

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:20.580
But what a relief.

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:22.500
This isn't a relief!

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.870
We can't blow him up with a fake.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:26.620
I'm glad it was a fake.

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:27.160
A real explosion would be dangerous!

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:28.790
So they DID get this from Pops' shop.

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:28.790
A real explosion would be dangerous!

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:29.160
So they DID get this from Pops' shop.

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:30.620
So they DID get this from Pops' shop.

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:30.620
Pops lied to us.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:31.080
Yeah, we were tricked!

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:33.080
That old man has everything.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:33.080
Yeah, we were tricked!

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:34.330
Yeah, we were tricked!

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:35.870
What? No!

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:36.540
Girls!

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:38.580
Let me show you something.

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:42.620
Things like this have something called a "safety."

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:44.580
A "safety"?

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:48.250
If you don't switch it off, the ammo won't fire.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:51.000
Oh, I see! So that's why!

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.160
Okay, now give it back!

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:54.500
Don't be stupid!

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:57.200
You snot-nosed brats

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:57.200
think I'd actually give it back to you?!

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:03.330
The tables have been turned!

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:05.790
I'm gonna blow you to smithereens!

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:07.200
Ya-hoo!

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:09.200
What?! R-reens?!

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:14.950
I... I don't wanna be reens!

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:16.620
It's "smithereens."

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:18.830
I am excellent at dodging.

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:22.120
I'm a tenth-degree licensed bare-handed blade stopper!

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:24.160
No, guys!

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:28.750
Be r-reen... smotherings with me!

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:29.500
Smotherings?

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:31.620
Don't worry.

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.660
You'll ALL be smothering by the time I'm done with you!

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:38.120
Stop!

00:13:38.870 --> 00:13:40.830
I'm calling a strategy meeting!

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:43.000
Oh? Alright.

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:44.080
Leader!

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:45.830
Strategy meeting!

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:49.040
Strategy meeting!

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:53.120
It's so light.

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.950
There's no way this is real.

00:13:56.870 --> 00:13:59.790
Wait. There's no telling with that old man.

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:02.950
They're running away!

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:04.500
Stop or I'll shoot!

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:06.330
You snot-nosed brats!

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:07.580
Time to be...

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:09.040
splattered across town!

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:10.750
Got it!

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:12.160
I-it really launched!

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:14.160
I caught it! I really caught it!

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:15.370
I really caught it!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:16.620
Cool!

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:19.080
Well, I AM an 11th-degree licensed

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:19.080
bare-handed blade stopper!

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.200
That's an extra degree.

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:21.250
Aren't I awesome?

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:22.540
Yeah, you ARE awesome!

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:24.620
Awesomely adorable?

00:14:24.620 --> 00:14:25.660
Uh-huh!

00:14:26.120 --> 00:14:26.910
What?

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:29.620
It might explode if you throw it at him.

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:32.250
It's not going to explode.

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:35.540
There was not enough recoil for this thing to be real.

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:36.910
Recoil?

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:40.160
Then you've shot a real rocket launcher before?

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:42.660
No.

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:46.160
Saito! Time to be slathered across town!

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:46.910
Stop!

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:50.620
I'm calling a strategy meeting.

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:52.450
No you aren't!

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:53.540
Stupid little-

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:58.250
Oh...

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:01.540
...my...

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:08.540
It IS a fake.

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:10.580
Aw, man, really?

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:13.500
Let's go get a different weapon from Pops!

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:14.330
Okay!

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.160
Well, well.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:23.200
"Well, well"... my ass.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.870
Please let them pick me.

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.080
What did you apply for, Yui?

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.910
A food dish for Colonel Monochrome.

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:43.830
You don't have a food dish, do you, Colonel?

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:47.540
Yui! Koto-chan!

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:48.750
We've got trouble!

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:50.540
Sat-chan, what's up?

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:51.870
A crapper!

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:54.750
Poop again?

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:57.120
Sat-chan, that's gross.

00:15:58.250 --> 00:15:59.540
Oops, my mistake.

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:01.950
It's not a crapper, it's a coffer.

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:03.450
But I did it on purpose!

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:05.830
Anyway, there's a coffer!

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:08.120
A safe, and it won't open!

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:09.910
A safe that won't open?

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:13.750
I wonder what's inside! Jewels? Treasure?

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:15.120
Maybe someone's pinky.

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:16.080
What?!

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:17.410
Or an ear.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:20.290
You're scaring me, Kotoha! That would be a crime!

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:22.660
If there's a crime, then we're on the case!

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:23.950
Let's go!

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:25.160
Yeah!

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:33.000
This is the safe that won't open.

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:34.450
That's awesome!

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:36.830
Is it from your shop, Pops?

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:38.160
Yeah.

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:42.950
I had it on the shelf for sale, but as you can see,

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:42.950
someone has locked it.

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:45.410
It won't open.

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:48.370
And you brought it all the way here.

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:51.660
So, Pops! Does that mean this is a case?

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:53.450
Hold it, brats.

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:55.620
What do you think YOU can do about it?

00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:57.200
We are...

00:16:57.580 --> 00:16:58.700
Colors!

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:01.250
We keep the peace in our town!

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:03.370
Yup! I know you can do it!

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:04.620
Yeah, yeah.

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:07.620
Okay, here.

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:09.000
You should have this.

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:12.000
It's a code from the culprit.

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:16.870
I've hidden a treasure

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:16.870
inside the safe

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:16.870
I am pan, a loaf stuffed

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:16.870
with everyone's love,

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:16.870
but you can't eat me. What am I? 

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:16.870
Hint: Look up from under me.

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:14.370
If you can crack the code,

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:16.910
I'll let you have the "treasure" inside the safe.

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:18.250
Treasure?!

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:19.870
You mean it, Pops?

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:21.080
Yup!

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:24.660
"Pan"! That's "bread"!

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:26.660
Bread you can't eat!

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:32.370
A loaf stuffed with love, but you can't eat it.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:32.370
What could it be?

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:35.160
The hint is to look up from under it.

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:37.200
The bakery! They sell pan there! Let's go!

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.040
Wait!

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.040
The bakery! They sell pan there! Let's go!

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:41.580
Well, I guess I'll go back to my shop.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:45.040
What are you doing, Saito?

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:49.330
If I start with 1 and try everything,

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:49.330
I'll get it open eventually.

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:51.750
You do things the boring way.

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:53.040
Bread!

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:54.750
Pan!

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:58.330
Pan! Pan! Pan seller! Bakery! Bread seller!

00:17:58.330 --> 00:18:00.160
Bread crumbs! Bread crap!

00:18:00.450 --> 00:18:02.750
Excuse me, do you have any crap?

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:06.000
Is this the bakery that sells the loaves no one can eat?

00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:29.330
They yelled at me a lot.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.450
Sorry. I couldn't follow you.

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:36.160
I don't think it had a single thing to do with crap.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.410
Let's go back to the hideout and come up with a plan.

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:40.370
Yeah.

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:42.500
But before that...

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:44.910
Stupidheads!

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:49.620
Let's see. Pan you can't eat.

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:57.120
Frying Pan

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:57.120
Panda

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:52.620
There's frying pan, and panda...

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:56.790
So we just need to find something like one of these

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:56.790
and look up from under it?

00:18:57.290 --> 00:18:58.700
Yui. May I?

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.040
Yes, Kotoha!

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:02.870
If you really want to, you CAN eat a panda.

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:04.540
That's true.

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:06.750
Pan you look up from under it...

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:08.830
Of course! I got it!

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:13.790
Yui's panties.

00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:15.290
Don't do that!

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:17.620
That hurts, Yui.

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:20.790
Oh, I'm sorry! But panties are...

00:19:21.040 --> 00:19:22.410
I want to do it, too.

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:24.500
What? No, Kotoha!

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:26.000
Alright, Koto-chan!

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:27.120
Go for it!

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:28.700
Oh, that.

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:31.830
Come on, be serious about this!

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:37.700
Pan you can't eat. Panties you can't eat.

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:37.700
Pandas you can't eat.

00:19:37.870 --> 00:19:40.160
You're just adding "you can't eat" to everything.

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:41.580
Wait, Sat-chan.

00:19:41.870 --> 00:19:43.160
What did you just say?

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:44.950
I said I'm super cute!

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:46.910
No you didn't.

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:50.790
What was it? Pandas you can't eat?

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:52.660
Oh. I've got it.

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:54.910
Kotoha?

00:19:57.540 --> 00:19:59.370
I've beat this game!

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:12.040
There it is!

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:13.870
Zoo Area

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:13.870
Police Satellite Station

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:13.700
I see.

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:16.830
"Everyone's love" meant "letters."

00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:19.370
And they were all "stuffed" in the panda mailbox.

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:21.750
The code for the safe was taped underneath it.

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:25.660
Well good for you.

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:28.540
Poor Saito, trying every code starting from 1.

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:30.120
Stupid Saito!

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:31.200
Shut up!

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:33.790
It's open!

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:34.830
What's in it?

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:37.330
Oh! This is...

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:40.250
Aw, it's not a pinky.

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:43.040
What is it?

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:45.160
There's a note inside, too!

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:47.950
Dear Colors

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:47.750
"Dear Colors...

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:51.540
Congratulations on opening the safe. It's me, Pops."

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:52.660
Pops?!

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:56.950
"Here is the food dish that Yui-chan wanted

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:56.950
for Colonel Monochrome."

00:20:57.200 --> 00:20:59.830
It was all Pops' scheme?

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:04.200
"And Saito, if you manage to open the safe first, 

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:06.200
just close it again and don't say anything."

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:07.580
That old geezer.

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:08.580
Here!

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:10.160
Huh? Oh.

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:12.200
Yay! A food dish!

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:16.410
Oh yeah, we WERE looking for one of those

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:16.410
at Pops's store the other day.

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:18.160
Treasure! It's our treasure!

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:24.370
Dear Saito,

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:24.370
Thanks for returning

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:24.370
the safe!

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:21.500
What? That rotten...

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:22.950
This thing is heavy!

00:21:22.950 --> 00:21:24.290
No, wait a minute.

00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:28.120
If you really look at it,

00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:28.120
it's not really "treasure" quality, is it?

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:30.950
You're right, there aren't any jewels on it.

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:33.080
Let's make Pops try again.

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:36.040
Wow. How bratty can you be?

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:55.620
Colonel Monochrome

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:29.660
Um, I call to order the Colors Evaluation Meeting!

00:23:29.660 --> 00:23:31.870
Evaluation meeting? What's that?

00:23:31.870 --> 00:23:34.410
Apparently an "evaluation meeting"

00:23:31.870 --> 00:23:34.410
is a preview for the next episode.

00:23:34.410 --> 00:23:36.580
N-no, it's not anything like-

00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:38.200
Oh. We're out of time.

00:23:38.200 --> 00:23:40.700
No way! Um... um, um...
